   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Aid</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF WASH Program and Monitoring Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The investment consists of two activities:
1.	$2.5 million (2018-2022) for UNICEF&#x2019;s strengthening of national WASH monitoring; and
support for improved monitoring of WASH in the Indo-Pacific region, through the UNICEF East Asia Pacific Regional Office (EAPRO). This includes country level support to Cambodia, Indonesia, PNG and Solomon Islands, as well as regional and global support to EAPRO countries. Support helps to produce reliable estimates of national, regional and global progress on water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) to inform decision making. 

2.	$6,002,640 for UNICEF&#x2019;s Climate Resilient Water, Sanitation and Hygiene program (2022-2025). 
The overall goal of this program is to ensure safe, sustainable, inclusive, and climate resilient water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) services, particularly among the poorest and most vulnerable children and their families. By the end of 2025, it is expected that 100,000 women, men, girls and boys will have access to climate-resilient WASH.</narrative>
  </description>
